# recitations.agg
# ======================================================================
#
# Every DecL program in *Recitations*, the book of textbook and
# examination problems worked with `aggregate`. Each declaration
# carries a note{} naming the text it comes from and the example or
# exercise it works.
#
# Generated from the book by `make_agg.py`; do not edit by hand. Programs
# are in canonical form, which is what the parser understood rather than
# what was typed, and are named `<CitationKey>.<declared name>` so that
# nothing in the file shadows anything else. Where more than three
# declarations share a shape, two are kept, as the book appendix samples
# them, and a model built by more than one chapter is listed once.
#
# 78 programs from 5 chapters.
#
# Read it back with `build.load("recitations.agg")`, or parse it
# without loading with `build.interpret_file("recitations.agg")`.
# Sections below are the book chapters that built the programs; the
# name and the note give the source.


# Bibliography
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The 5 works the notes below cite, read from the library
# the book itself cites, D:/Projects/Biblio/uber-library.bib.
#
# @Bahnemann2015
#     Bahnemann, David (2015). Distributions for Actuaries. Casualty
#     Actuarial Society Monographs No. 2. www.casact.org
#
# @Bodoff2007
#     Bodoff, Neil M. (2007). Capital Allocation by Percentile Layer.
#     Variance 3(1), 13-30.
#
# @Brehm2007
#     Brehm, Paul J. and Perry, James H. and Venter, Gary G. and Witcraft,
#     Susan E. (2007). Enterprise Risk Analysis. Casualty Actuarial
#     Society.
#
# @Frees2018a
#     Frees, Edward (2018). Loss Data Analytics. Open Actuarial Texts.
#     https://openacttexts.github.io/Loss-Data-Analytics/
#
# @Klugman2019
#     Klugman, Stuart A. and Panjer, Harry H. and Willmot, Gordon E.
#     (2019). Loss Models: from data to decisions. John Wiley & Sons.
#

# Loss Models, Chapter 9  [Klugman2019.qmd]
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

agg Klugman2019.KPW.95
